```\nWait! Is there a required `findings.json` file or where should `findings.json` be? Wait! Let's re-read the prompt description for required deliverables:\n\nDeliverables:\nWrite all five files to `/app`. A run that produces fewer than five is scored as incomplete, not as a low score.\n\n1. `progress.md`: Investigation timeline and working checklist\n2. `intrusion-report.md`: Attack chain, evidence, entities, persistence, impact\n3. `vuln-report.md`: Vulnerability-driven entry analysis (or its explicit absence)\n4. `baseline-report.md`: Baseline / configuration weaknesses\n5. `remediation-plan.md`: Prioritised, correct, complete, verifiable plan\n\nWait! Let's check if `findings.json` or `change-ticket.md` or anything else needs to be updated or if `findings.json` or `change-ticket.md` are expected or if modifying `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` or placing `change-ticket.md` somewhere is mentioned in the prompt text.\n\nLet's carefully check the text in prompt and `/sas/handoff`:\nIn `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`:\n\"> A previous shift pre-filled this remediation ticket from the SAS alerts ALONE. It is known\n> to be incomplete and contains stale/incorrect lines. Correct it IN PLACE against your own\n> investigation of /disk; cite evidence for every change. Do not author from scratch.\"\nWait! \"Correct it IN PLACE\" - wait, is `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` writable? Let's check if `/sas` is writable!",
